    "case_for": "This is a major realization of Mingus's large-ensemble ambition: original compositions rendered on a symphonic scale while retaining the blues, swing, volatility, and collective force central to his work. The dossier identifies praise from AllMusic, DownBeat, and the Rolling Stone Jazz Record Guide, and reports that Mingus named it his favorite of his recordings. Its four 1971 sessions assembled extraordinary personnel\u2014Dannie Richmond, Jimmy Knepper, Jaki Byard, Charles McPherson, James Moody, Roland Hanna, and a bass contingent including Ron Carter, Richard Davis, and Milt Hinton\u2014giving the date exceptional session gravity (S1, S3, S4).",
